From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: rk8xx: restart the RK817 through PSCI, as the vendor kernel

A PMIC reset power-cycles the SoC and clears PMU_GRF_OS_REG0, where the
reboot-mode driver leaves the flag U-Boot reads: "reboot charge" then boots
the system again instead of charge mode.

---
--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
@@ -883,7 +883,6 @@
 
 		switch (rk808->variant) {
 		case RK809_ID:
-		case RK817_ID:
 			ret = devm_register_sys_off_handler(dev,
 							    SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART, SYS_OFF_PRIO_HIGH,
 							    &rk808_restart, rk808);
